   "op": "replace_brief",
   "brief": "voices",
   "html": "<div class=\"brief sp\" id=\"voices\" data-entry=\"hub\" data-lens=\"psych\" data-spine=\"2\" data-shelf=\"psych\" data-bp=\"behav\">\n<h4>Hears Voices or Holds Odd Beliefs</h4>\n<p class=\"sub\">primary psychosis &middot; psychosis inside mood episodes &middot; personality traits &middot; normal and developmental &middot; trauma, drugs and illness<span class=\"subq\">Persistent psychosis, or mood, a drug, an illness, a trauma disorder or a lifelong trait?</span></p>\n<nav class=\"sp-step\" aria-label=\"Decision spine\"><a href=\"#vo-s1\"><b>1</b><span>Presentation</span></a><a href=\"#vo-s2\"><b>2</b><span>Urgent</span></a><a href=\"#vo-dx\"><b>3</b><span>Differential</span></a><a href=\"#vo-s4\"><b>4</b><span>Workup</span></a><a class=\"off\" aria-disabled=\"true\" title=\"Not used in this brief\"><b>5</b><span>Criteria</span></a><a class=\"off\" aria-disabled=\"true\" title=\"Not used in this brief\"><b>6</b><span>Severity</span></a><a class=\"off\" aria-disabled=\"true\" title=\"Not used in this brief\"><b>7</b><span>Treatment</span></a><a class=\"off\" aria-disabled=\"true\" title=\"Not used in this brief\"><b>8</b><span>Follow-up</span></a><a href=\"#vo-bank\" class=\"sp-prac\"><span>Practice</span></a></nav>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"vo-s1\"><b class=\"sp-n\">1</b>Presentation</h5>\n<div class=\"dp\"><span class=\"lbl\">Bottom line</span><ul class=\"bl\"><li>First rule out a drug or a medical illness, including delirium; a trauma disorder alone does not typically explain psychosis</li><li>Then: does the psychosis persist, and is it only inside mood episodes?</li><li>Lifelong odd traits that may include odd perceptions, with no persistent psychosis <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> a personality disorder</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"sp-script sp-s2\"><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">What it is</span><div class=\"sv\"><p>Psychosis: a distorted perception of reality, with delusions, hallucinations or disorganized thought or speech</p></div></div><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Sort by</span><div class=\"sv\"><p>Cause (drug, illness, trauma) <span class=\"op op-p\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"and\"></span> course (persistent, inside mood episodes, lifelong traits)</p></div></div><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Hands off</span><div class=\"sv\"><p>Timing and treatment of each psychotic disorder: Psychosis; a manic episode: Bipolar Disorder; a drug or disease: Psychiatric Symptoms from Medical Illness or Medication</p></div></div></div>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"vo-s2\"><b class=\"sp-n\">2</b>Urgent risks</h5>\n<div class=\"sp-rows\">\n<div class=\"sp-row\"><span class=\"sp-src\">Delirium</span><b class=\"sp-f\">Fluctuating attention and disorientation; any psychosis is secondary</b><div class=\"sp-chips\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"delirium\">Delirium</button></div><p class=\"sp-commit\"><b>If</b> attention fails over hours to days, <b>choose</b> <span class=\"mask\">find and treat the drug or illness causing it</span>.</p></div>\n<div class=\"sp-row\"><span class=\"sp-src\">Drug or illness</span><b class=\"sp-f\">A new medication, drug use or a disease known to cause psychosis</b><div class=\"sp-chips\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"psych-medical\">Psychiatric Symptoms from Medical Illness or Medication</button></div><p class=\"sp-commit\"><b>If</b> the timing ties it to a drug or disease, <b>choose</b> <span class=\"mask\">treat the cause before naming a primary disorder</span>.</p></div>\n</div>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"vo-dx\"><b class=\"sp-n\">3</b>Differential</h5>\n<div class=\"sp-dx\"><table class=\"dense\"><caption>Which look-alike, most tempting first</caption><thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Fingerprint</th><th>Decides it</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"psychosis-duration\">Primary psychotic disorder</button></td><td><span>Delusions or voices that persist</span></td><td><span><b>How long</b>: under 1 month brief, 1 to under 6 months schizophreniform, 6 months or more schizophrenia</span></td></tr><tr><td><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"bipolar-mania\">Mood with psychosis</button></td><td><span>Discrete mood episodes</span></td><td><span><b>Psychosis only inside a mood episode</b></span></td></tr><tr><td>Delusional disorder</td><td><span>One or more delusions; no prominent voices or disorganization</span></td><td><span><b>1 month or more</b>; works and behaves normally apart from the delusion</span></td></tr><tr><td>Personality disorder</td><td><span>Schizotypal: odd beliefs, <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"vo-pop-1\">magical thinking</button><span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"vo-pop-1\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">Short of delusions</span>Superstition or clairvoyance, suspiciousness and paranoid ideas can occur but are not of delusional intensity. Flat affect with odd beliefs short of delusions, and no other prominent psychotic symptoms, is not schizophrenia</span>, typically few friends from social anxiety that familiarity does not ease; paranoid: distrust; schizoid: detached</span></td><td><span><b>Lifelong</b>, with no persistent psychosis</span></td></tr><tr><td><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"cluster-b\">Borderline personality disorder</button></td><td><span>Paranoia or voices under stress</span></td><td><span><b>Under 24 hours</b>; unstable relationships and mood, self-harm</span></td></tr><tr><td>After a trauma</td><td><span>Acute stress disorder or PTSD (posttraumatic stress disorder)</span></td><td><span><b>Psychosis is not part of either</b>; voices a week after a stressor point to brief psychotic disorder</span></td></tr><tr><td>Developmental and normal</td><td><span><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"vo-pop-2\">Imaginary friend</button><span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"vo-pop-2\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">Reassure</span>A child with friends and good function needs reassurance; with no anxiety disorder, therapy is not necessary. The companion can help the child master anxiety and build competence. Pretend play, dress-up and fanciful storytelling are also normal in young children.</span> (healthy; most common at 3 to 6, can last into school age; aids creativity and rehearses social skills, with no harm to real friendships); autism spectrum disorder</span></td><td><span><b>No withdrawal or fall in function</b>; autism has no hallucinations</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<figure class=\"lcw lcc\" data-mimic-hub=\"voices\" data-mimic-full=\"1\"><div class=\"ttl\"><span>Hears Voices or Holds Odd Beliefs</span><small>not to scale</small></div><ol class=\"wrows\"><li class=\"wgb\"><p class=\"wg\">Primary psychotic</p><ol class=\"wrows\"><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"schizophrenia\" data-mrow-v=\"26fa3be05849\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Schizophrenia</b><span class=\"win\">6 months or more in all</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs pro\" style=\"--a:30%;--b:38%\"></i><i class=\"cs act\" style=\"--a:38%;--b:46%\"></i><i class=\"cs res\" style=\"--a:46%;--b:100%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs pro\"></i>Prodrome</span><span><i class=\"cs act\"></i>Active psychosis</span><span><i class=\"cs res\"></i>Residual</span></p><p class=\"wl\">Onset late teens to 20s, often after a prodrome</p><p class=\"wl\">2 or more, at least 1 of delusions, voices or disorganized speech</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Functioning falls and stays below baseline</p></div></li><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"schizophreniform\" data-mrow-v=\"c3a500f033ef\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Schizophreniform disorder</b><span class=\"win\">1 to under 6 months</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs act\" style=\"--a:40%;--b:46%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs act\"></i>Active psychosis</span></p><p class=\"wl\">Same symptoms as schizophrenia</p><p class=\"wl\">Functional decline not required</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Under 6 months in all</p></div></li><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"brief-psychotic\" data-mrow-v=\"34098c5fbd8d\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Brief psychotic disorder</b><span class=\"win\">1 day to under 1 month</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs act\" style=\"--a:70%;--b:72%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs act\"></i>Active psychosis</span></p><p class=\"wl\">Sudden onset, often after a marked stressor</p><p class=\"wl\">1 or more: delusions, voices, disorganization</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Full return to baseline within a month</p></div></li><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"schizoaffective\" data-mrow-v=\"436b2bdd5750\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Schizoaffective disorder</b><span class=\"win\">Psychosis 2 weeks or more without mood</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs lop\" style=\"--a:40%;--b:50%\"></i><i class=\"cs act\" style=\"--a:50%;--b:54%\"></i><i class=\"cs lop\" style=\"--a:54%;--b:66%\"></i><i class=\"cs act\" style=\"--a:66%;--b:70%\"></i><i class=\"cs lop\" style=\"--a:70%;--b:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs act\" style=\"--a:84%;--b:88%\"></i><i class=\"cs lop\" style=\"--a:88%;--b:100%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs lop\"></i>Depressive episode with psychosis</span><span><i class=\"cs act\"></i>Active psychosis</span></p><p class=\"wl\">A major mood episode at the same time as the active psychosis</p><p class=\"wl\">Delusions or voices 2 weeks or more with no mood episode</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Mood episodes fill most of the illness</p></div></li><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"delusional\" data-mrow-v=\"58004a615104\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Delusional disorder</b><span class=\"win\">1 month or more</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs only\" style=\"--a:80%;--b:100%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs only\"></i>A delusion only</span></p><p class=\"wl\">Often begins around 40</p><p class=\"wl\">One or more delusions; no prominent voices or disorganization</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Works and behaves normally apart from the delusion</p></div></li></ol></li><li class=\"wgb\"><p class=\"wg\">Mood with psychosis</p><ol class=\"wrows\"><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"mdd-psychotic\" data-mrow-v=\"8fbc9f765fc1\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Major depressive disorder with psychotic features</b><span class=\"win\">Episodes 2 weeks or more</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs lo\" style=\"--a:39%;--b:46%\"></i><i class=\"cs lop\" style=\"--a:61%;--b:68%\"></i><i class=\"cs lo\" style=\"--a:81%;--b:88%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs lo\"></i>Depressive episode</span><span><i class=\"cs lop\"></i>Depressive episode with psychosis</span></p><p class=\"wl\">Discrete depressive episodes</p><p class=\"wl\">Low mood or anhedonia, sleep and appetite change</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Psychosis only inside a depressive episode</p></div></li><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"bipolar-psychotic\" data-mrow-v=\"aec56d40cb00\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Bipolar I disorder with psychotic features</b><span class=\"win\">Mania 1 week or more, or any length if hospitalized</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs hi\" style=\"--a:34%;--b:41%\"></i><i class=\"cs hip\" style=\"--a:55%;--b:62%\"></i><i class=\"cs hi\" style=\"--a:76%;--b:83%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs hi\"></i>Manic episode</span><span><i class=\"cs hip\"></i>Manic episode with psychosis</span></p><p class=\"wl\">Discrete manic episodes; depression common</p><p class=\"wl\">Elated or irritable mood, less sleep, pressured speech</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Psychosis only inside a mood episode</p></div></li></ol></li><li class=\"wgb\"><p class=\"wg\">Personality: no persistent psychosis</p><ol class=\"wrows\"><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"paranoid-pd\" data-mrow-v=\"a041e98f97f4\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Paranoid personality disorder</b><span class=\"win\">Lifelong, from adolescence or early adulthood</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs trait\" style=\"--a:24%;--b:100%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs trait\"></i>Lifelong trait, no psychosis</span></p><p class=\"wl\">Suspicious, distrustful, hypervigilant</p><p class=\"wl\">No odd beliefs, magical thinking or eccentric speech</p><p class=\"wl dec\">No period of persistent delusions or hallucinations</p></div></li><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"schizoid-pd\" data-mrow-v=\"f2104b715e54\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Schizoid personality disorder</b><span class=\"win\">Lifelong, from adolescence or early adulthood</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs trait\" style=\"--a:24%;--b:100%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs trait\"></i>Lifelong trait, no psychosis</span></p><p class=\"wl\">Prefers to be alone; detached, little emotion</p><p class=\"wl\">No odd beliefs or eccentric behavior</p><p class=\"wl dec\">No hallucinations or delusions</p></div></li><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"schizotypal-pd\" data-mrow-v=\"291a05e015e6\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Schizotypal personality disorder</b><span class=\"win\">Lifelong, from adolescence or early adulthood</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs odd\" style=\"--a:24%;--b:100%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs odd\"></i>Lifelong odd beliefs, no psychosis</span></p><p class=\"wl\">Odd beliefs, magical thinking, eccentric dress and speech</p><p class=\"wl\">Few close relationships; paranoid ideas common</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Odd perceptions short of frank psychosis, not persistent</p></div></li><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"borderline-pd\" data-mrow-v=\"770b360c15e4\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Borderline personality disorder</b><span class=\"win\">Stress psychosis is brief and transient</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs trait\" style=\"--a:24%;--b:100%\"></i><i class=\"cs mark\" style=\"--x:44%\"></i><i class=\"cs mark\" style=\"--x:66%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs trait\"></i>Lifelong trait, no psychosis</span><span><i class=\"cs mark\"></i>Stress psychosis, minutes to hours</span></p><p class=\"wl\">Unstable relationships and mood; impulsivity, self-harm</p><p class=\"wl\">Paranoia or voices under stress</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Temporary; usually short of a separate disorder</p></div></li></ol></li><li class=\"wgb\"><p class=\"wg\">Developmental and normal</p><ol class=\"wrows\"><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"autism\" data-mrow-v=\"244e4711ff2e\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Autism spectrum disorder</b><span class=\"win\">From the early developmental period</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs dev\" style=\"--a:0%;--b:100%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs dev\"></i>Developmental, from early childhood</span></p><p class=\"wl\">Persistent deficits in social communication</p><p class=\"wl\">Restricted, repetitive behaviors or interests</p><p class=\"wl dec\">No hallucinations; any skill loss is in early childhood</p></div></li><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"imaginary-friend\" data-mrow-v=\"58816504bea4\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Imaginary friend (normal)</b><span class=\"win\">Common in preschool and school age</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs norm\" style=\"--a:0%;--b:18%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs norm\"></i>Normal at that age</span></p><p class=\"wl\">A companion in early childhood</p><p class=\"wl\">No withdrawal and no fall in function</p><p class=\"wl dec\">A voice with decline in a teen suggests a hallucination</p></div></li></ol></li><li class=\"wgb\"><p class=\"wg\">After a trauma</p><ol class=\"wrows\"><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"acute-stress\" data-mrow-v=\"7c92af43b415\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Acute stress disorder</b><span class=\"win\">3 days to 1 month after a trauma</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs stress\" style=\"--a:50%;--b:52%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs stress\"></i>Trauma symptoms, no psychosis</span></p><p class=\"wl\">Follows a traumatic event</p><p class=\"wl\">9 or more: intrusion, negative mood, dissociation, avoidance, arousal</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Psychosis is not part of the criteria</p></div></li><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"ptsd\" data-mrow-v=\"99020a57f4b5\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Posttraumatic stress disorder</b><span class=\"win\">Symptoms last over 1 month; onset can be delayed</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs stress\" style=\"--a:50%;--b:62%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs stress\"></i>Trauma symptoms, no psychosis</span></p><p class=\"wl\">Follows a traumatic event</p><p class=\"wl\">Intrusions, avoidance, negative mood, arousal</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Lasts over a month; psychosis is not typical</p></div></li></ol></li><li class=\"wgb\"><p class=\"wg\">A drug or illness</p><ol class=\"wrows\"><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"substance-psychosis\" data-mrow-v=\"08e92d1a147c\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Substance-induced psychotic disorder</b><span class=\"win\">During or soon after use</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs sub\" style=\"--a:40%;--b:43%\"></i><i class=\"cs sub\" style=\"--a:54%;--b:57%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs sub\"></i>Psychosis tied to a drug</span></p><p class=\"wl\">Drug use shown by history, exam or labs</p><p class=\"wl\">Delusions or hallucinations</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Usually remits once use stops</p></div></li><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"medication-psychosis\" data-mrow-v=\"19da18d49526\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Medication-induced psychotic disorder</b><span class=\"win\">Begins with a new medication</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs sub\" style=\"--a:84%;--b:86%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs sub\"></i>Psychosis tied to a drug</span></p><p class=\"wl\">A new medication, eg, high-dose glucocorticoids</p><p class=\"wl\">Acute delusions or hallucinations</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Alert and oriented; timing ties it to the drug</p></div></li><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"medical-psychosis\" data-mrow-v=\"239d6d3731f9\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Psychotic disorder due to another medical condition</b><span class=\"win\">Begins and ends with the illness</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs ill\" style=\"--a:88%;--b:90%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs ill\"></i>Psychosis tied to an illness</span></p><p class=\"wl\">A disease known to cause psychosis (eg, brain tumor, thyroid storm)</p><p class=\"wl\">History, examination or labs show the disease</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Treating the disease often eases the psychosis</p></div></li><li class=\"cr\" data-mrow=\"delirium\" data-mrow-v=\"44089d87b0dd\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Delirium</b><span class=\"win\">Hours to days; fluctuates</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail cstrip\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:20%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:38%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:62%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:84%\"></i><i class=\"cs flux\" style=\"--a:90%;--b:92%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">Child</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:20%\">Teens</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:38%\">20s</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:62%\">30s</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:84%\">40s+</span></div><p class=\"rk\"><span><i class=\"cs flux\"></i>Fluctuating attention (delirium)</span></p><p class=\"wl\">A drug or illness as the cause</p><p class=\"wl\">Fluctuating attention and disorientation; any psychosis is secondary</p><p class=\"wl dec\">Attention fails over hours to days</p></div></li></ol></li></ol></figure>\n<h5 class=\"tsec sp-h\" id=\"vo-s4\"><b class=\"sp-n\">4</b>Workup</h5>\n<figure class=\"lcp w5a\"><p class=\"kick\">Diagnostic workup</p><p class=\"w5z\">First step</p><div class=\"w5t first\"><div class=\"w5b\"><div class=\"w5c\">New voices or odd beliefs</div><span class=\"w5ar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&rarr;</span><div class=\"w5o\"><span class=\"mask w5om\"><span class=\"w5ol\">Medication and substance history, with timing</span><span class=\"w5ol\">Chemistry, blood count, liver and thyroid tests, vitamin B12, urine drug screen, urinalysis, HIV (human immunodeficiency virus) serology</span></span></div></div><div class=\"w5f\"><div class=\"w5fd f1\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">A drug, a disease or delirium</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an f1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m f1\"><span class=\"mask\">Treat the cause first</span></div><div class=\"w5fd fl\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">No cause found</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an fl\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m fl\"><span class=\"mask\">Sort by the course</span></div></div></div><p class=\"w5z\">Next step</p><div class=\"w5t\"><div class=\"w5b\"><div class=\"w5c\">No cause found</div><span class=\"w5ar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&rarr;</span><div class=\"w5o\"><span class=\"mask w5om\"><span class=\"w5ol\">Course of the symptoms</span></span></div></div><div class=\"w5f\"><div class=\"w5fd f1\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">Persistent delusions or voices</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an f1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m f1\"><span class=\"mask\">Primary psychotic disorder: time it</span></div><div class=\"w5fd\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">Only inside a mood episode</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m\"><span class=\"mask\">Mood disorder with psychotic features</span></div><div class=\"w5fd\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">Hours, under stress</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m\"><span class=\"mask\">Borderline personality disorder</span></div><div class=\"w5fd fl\"><span class=\"t\" lang=\"en\">Lifelong traits, no frank psychosis</span><span class=\"ld\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></div><span class=\"w5an fl\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><div class=\"w5m fl\"><span class=\"mask\">A personality disorder</span></div></div></div><p class=\"w5skip\"><span class=\"w5z\">Skip</span><span class=\"mask\">No test sorts the primary look-alikes; the course does.</span></p></figure>\n<div class=\"sp-dx\"><table class=\"dense\"><caption>Clues that change the answer</caption><thead><tr><th>Clue</th><th>Points to</th><th>Next move</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A young child who sees and hears a companion, with organized speech and behavior</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">A normal imaginary friend</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Reassure; no referral or therapy</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>A teen whose voice comes with withdrawal and falling grades; or disorganization, isolation or lost milestones; or hallucinations in an older child</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">A hallucination, not an imaginary friend</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Psychiatric evaluation; time the psychosis<div class=\"sp-chips\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"psychosis-duration\">Psychosis</button></div></span></span></td></tr><tr><td>High-functioning with one fixed belief</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Delusional disorder</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Low function points to schizophrenia</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Elated or irritable mood, less sleep, pressured speech</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Mania with psychotic features</span></span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"bipolar-mania\">Bipolar Disorder</button></span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p class=\"sp-pause\"><b>Pause point.</b> The bait: schizophrenia for lifelong odd beliefs with no persistent psychosis, or for voices that pass within hours under stress. Persistence decides it.</p>\n\n<h5 class=\"authored-hdr\" id=\"vo-bank\">Practice</h5>\n<ol class=\"bank authored\">\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Imaginary friend (normal)\" data-d2=\"Autism spectrum disorder\" data-item-id=\"q_e997d08bdbede2325ba6\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_9fa05ff6f85032b12173\" data-d1-id=\"o_a7aa69406c132f1794e2\" data-d2-id=\"o_22028f69d5ab7559f124\" data-src=\"authored\" data-lead-in=\"Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\"><span class=\"sl\">15-year-old girl, 7 months of talking to \"Mira,\" a girl only she can hear</span>\n<span class=\"si\">sure her classmates are plotting against her</span>\n<span class=\"si\">grades fell; quit soccer; stays in her room; normal early development</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">urine toxicology negative &middot; T 36.8 °C</span> &rarr; <b>Schizophrenia</b> &rarr; a voice and a persecutory belief for over 6 months with a fall in function in a teenager: schizophrenia; a normal imaginary companion comes without withdrawal or decline, and autism dates from the early developmental period and has no hallucinations</li>\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Paranoid personality disorder\" data-d2=\"Schizophrenia\" data-item-id=\"q_28f93eaeabb48af3e64d\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_9405a9fd0895588a0024\" data-d1-id=\"o_1594583ef4a6c4bfc8f3\" data-d2-id=\"o_7426c1de50fe25b579ce\" data-src=\"authored\" data-lead-in=\"Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\"><span class=\"sl\">26-year-old man, since his teens believes he can sense others' thoughts</span>\n<span class=\"si\">wears odd, mismatched outfits; speaks in vague, odd phrases</span>\n<span class=\"ss\">few close friends; works steadily as a night clerk</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">no hallucinations or fixed delusions &middot; BP 120/78 mm Hg</span> &rarr; <b>Schizotypal personality disorder</b> &rarr; lifelong magical thinking, eccentric dress and speech and few relationships, short of frank psychosis: schizotypal; paranoid personality has distrust without odd beliefs, and schizophrenia needs persistent psychosis with a fall in function</li>\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Delusional disorder\" data-d2=\"Schizotypal personality disorder\" data-item-id=\"q_2d2d510ddaadd15be536\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_904280625e7ad9f6ba30\" data-d1-id=\"o_28bc74fdb30ea4914083\" data-d2-id=\"o_bf905a42c388ced921a2\" data-src=\"authored\" data-lead-in=\"Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\"><span class=\"sl\">48-year-old man, distrustful of coworkers since early adulthood</span>\n<span class=\"si\">suspects they exploit him; reads threats into harmless remarks</span>\n<span class=\"ss\">no odd beliefs or eccentric habits; no voices</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">no fixed false belief despite evidence &middot; BP 128/80 mm Hg</span> &rarr; <b>Paranoid personality disorder</b> &rarr; lifelong suspicion and hypervigilance with no persistent delusion or hallucination: paranoid personality disorder; delusional disorder needs one or more delusions for a month or more, and schizotypal adds odd beliefs and eccentricity</li>\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Schizotypal personality disorder\" data-d2=\"Autism spectrum disorder\" data-item-id=\"q_125ed48015246d7ea9ad\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_fa43a783dc9973634095\" data-d1-id=\"o_b7b4b287a43c40cce451\" data-d2-id=\"o_8b39308b0e064028031e\" data-src=\"authored\" data-lead-in=\"Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\"><span class=\"sl\">34-year-old man, always prefers solitary work and has no close friends</span>\n<span class=\"si\">indifferent to praise; shows little emotion</span>\n<span class=\"ss\">no odd beliefs or eccentric behavior; normal early development</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">no voices or delusions &middot; BP 118/76 mm Hg</span> &rarr; <b>Schizoid personality disorder</b> &rarr; a lifelong preference for being alone with detachment and little emotion, without odd beliefs: schizoid; schizotypal adds odd beliefs and eccentricity, and autism starts in the early developmental period with restricted, repetitive behaviors</li>\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Bipolar I disorder with psychotic features\" data-d2=\"Delusional disorder\" data-item-id=\"q_ee645dd4049c56c98a42\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_3eeaf0f7e4294d18a06e\" data-d1-id=\"o_9b9b0b2c3ac9d10b1fb1\" data-d2-id=\"o_474af3dc885274c5156d\" data-src=\"authored\" data-lead-in=\"Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\"><span class=\"sl\">24-year-old man, 9 months of believing he is a hidden prince</span>\n<span class=\"si\">speech jumps between unrelated topics; stopped working</span>\n<span class=\"ss\">mood even; sleeps 8 hours a night; no drug use</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">urine toxicology negative &middot; T 36.7 °C</span> &rarr; <b>Schizophrenia</b> &rarr; a grandiose delusion with disorganized speech for over 6 months and a fall in function: schizophrenia; in bipolar disorder the psychosis sits inside a mood episode, and delusional disorder has no prominent disorganization</li>\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Brief psychotic disorder\" data-d2=\"Schizophreniform disorder\" data-item-id=\"q_96f08a5f0ee0a06d44f4\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_c386e2ae9c7c0c1e81e0\" data-d1-id=\"o_18a6b4fee041ba406ce1\" data-d2-id=\"o_f79c9336c29afd54801f\" data-src=\"authored\" data-lead-in=\"Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\"><span class=\"sl\">23-year-old woman heard a voice calling her worthless for 3 hours after a breakup</span>\n<span class=\"si\">years of stormy relationships, mood swings and cutting</span>\n<span class=\"ss\">back to her usual self by evening</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">no drug use &middot; HR 84/min</span> &rarr; <b>Borderline personality disorder</b> &rarr; a voice under stress lasting hours, on a background of unstable relationships, mood and self-harm: borderline personality disorder; brief psychotic disorder needs at least 1 day, and schizophreniform at least 1 month</li>\n</ol>\n\n<div class=\"pearls\"><span class=\"lbl\">Pairs with</span> <b>Psychosis</b>: timing and treatment of each psychotic disorder. <b>Bipolar Disorder</b>: is there a manic episode? <b>Psychiatric Symptoms from Medical Illness or Medication</b>: did a drug or disease start it?</div>\n\n<div class=\"rule\"><span class=\"lbl\">Transferable rule</span><p>After ruling out a drug or a medical illness, decide whether the psychosis persists, whether it lives only inside mood episodes, and how long it has lasted.</p></div>\n\n</div>",
   "ledger": "repair/migration/psych/HUB/voices/spine/claim_map.json",
   "note": "decision spine v2: voices"
  }
 ]
}